<title>USA: Chester Valley Bancorp sets 5-for-4 split.</title>
<headline>Chester Valley Bancorp sets 5-for-4 split.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNINGTON, Pa. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chester Valley Bancorp Inc said on Monday it set a five-for-four stock split to be paid on March 19 to shareholders of record as of March 5.</p>
<p>The company also said it will continue to pay its regular quarterly dividend of $0.11 per share.  The stock split is expected to increase future dividends by 25 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>Chester Valley is the parent of First Financial Savings Bank. Chester Valley has assets of $290.17 million.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
